    <!-- Build QA -->
    <article class="wrap beat" aria-labelledby="qa-title">
      <h3 id="qa-title" class="beat-title">Checking every build against the designs</h3>
      <div class="prose-narrow">
        <p>Handing off the designs wasn’t the end of it. Leading up to release, I ran UX QA on the actual dev builds, checking each one side by side with the Figma files. I flagged everything from card shadows and footer blur to pixelated buttons, MFA icons and empty states, and included the CSS and type specs the engineers needed to fix each one.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="column-shot">
