    <!-- Desktop -->
    <article class="wrap beat" aria-labelledby="desktop-title">
      <h3 id="desktop-title" class="beat-title">Taking it back to the desktop</h3>
      <div class="prose-narrow">
        <p>The mobile patterns turned out to be useful beyond the phone. Partway through the project, I explored how they could scale back up to the desktop as a lighter, quick-response help desk: an activity chart of the week’s directory events above the same urgent counts, and a user page that leads with what’s wrong, like a locked-out banner with its own Unlock button, followed by the same quick actions as the app. It was a much smaller tool than the full Admin Portal, built for getting in, fixing something and getting out.</p>
      </div>
